dialogue still_party_talk
title: What the tanks hold
trigger: ThemeStart still
speaker commander $commander
speaker trusted $trusted
speaker enchantress - name=Enchantress portrait=whitewitch

node a commander
  The Still. I woke in one of these tanks. I think I died in one, too.
  -> b

node b enchantress
  You did. They were Halcyon's tanks, and now the Choir runs the tithe through them. That's what brought you back: colour taken from the holds. The Innkeeper found her village's in the next tank.
  -> c

node c commander
  Then I'm alive on their colour. And there's more here than any Lullaby needs. I can feel it.
  -> d

node d enchantress
  The rest goes up the spire. To someone who's been drinking it for a very long time.
  * You haven't said a word since the tanks. Say it. -> speak
    if: TrustAtLeast $trusted 25
  * Then that's where we go.

node speak trusted
  Somewhere in those tanks is colour from a village I know. Maybe some of it is in you now. I should hate that. I don't. If it had to go somewhere, I'm glad it went into someone who'd come back here and ask where the rest went.
  * Then I'll spend it well. On getting the rest back. -> spend
    do: AddTrust $trusted 6
  * I'll carry it carefully. Tell me whose it was, when you're ready. -> carry
    do: AddTrust $trusted 5

node spend trusted
  Spend it well. That's all I'd ask of anyone.

node carry trusted
  When I'm ready. Not today. But thank you for asking.
